# Auto detect text files and perform LF normalization
* text=auto

# D164: CRLF in a .py uploaded via WinSCP Binary lands \r on the VPS. Pin to LF.
# (The `*.py` line below appeared TWICE until S189 -- deduplicated here, and
#  recorded rather than silently fixed. Harmless, but a rule stated twice is a
#  rule nobody re-read.)
*.py  text eol=lf
*.sh  text eol=lf

# S189: D164 stopped at .py and .sh. Every HTML kit since S179 has reached the
# VPS correctly by Linux convention rather than by rule -- that is luck, not a
# guarantee. `.new` is the extension every kit stages a replacement page under.
*.html text eol=lf
*.new  text eol=lf
*.sql  text eol=lf

# S192: the same gap, one layer further out -- the files that GATE an install.
# PUBLISH_ALL warned that `KIT_ID.txt` and `SUMS.md5` "will be replaced by CRLF
# the next time Git touches it". A CRLF `SUMS.md5` makes `md5sum -c` read the
# filename as `staff_ledger_X.py\r`, fail to find it, and turn a PERFECTLY GOOD
# kit RED at gate [1/6] -- a halt that fires wrongly, which is worse than no
# halt at all, because a halt that always fires gets waved through (D316).
# `live_pins.txt` is read on the VPS by verify_live_pins.py for the same reason.
# Nothing had broken when this was added: the warning was the finding.
# Kin of F-100 (the .gitignore blanket that silently dropped a kit file).
*.md5 text eol=lf
*.txt text eol=lf
